From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonid Komarianskyi <leonid_komarianskyi@epam.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Feb 2026 15:07:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pci-host: gpex: shrink memory region from 256MB to 128MB
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Since we are not using the standard full ECAM size of 256MB, and the
base address for virtio PCI on R-Car setups starts from 0x33000000, the
memory region overlaps with GUEST_RAM0_BASE (0x40000000). This overlap
causes issues when trying to utilize the memory region
[0x40000000–0x43000000], for example, when loading Android images from
U-Boot. As we are using the PCI range [0x33000000–0x3a800000], which
fits within a 128MB length, the memory region can be reduced from 256MB
to 128MB.

(cherry picked from commit 90cc72e21366022be94ce68ccd52548ba0012afa)

Signed-off-by: Leonid Komarianskyi <leonid_komarianskyi@epam.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream fork / BSP-layer delta; not submitted upstream]
Origin: https://github.com/xen-troops/qemu commit 90cc72e21366022be94ce68ccd52548ba0012afa
---
 hw/pci-host/gpex.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/pci-host/gpex.c b/hw/pci-host/gpex.c
index e66784ce5..fc509d778 100644
--- a/hw/pci-host/gpex.c
+++ b/hw/pci-host/gpex.c
@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@ static void gpex_host_realize(DeviceState *dev, Error **errp)
 
     s->irq = g_malloc0_n(s->num_irqs, sizeof(*s->irq));
 
-    pcie_host_mmcfg_init(pex, PCIE_MMCFG_SIZE_MAX);
+    pcie_host_mmcfg_init(pex, PCIE_MMCFG_SIZE_MAX/2);
     sysbus_init_mmio(sbd, &pex->mmio);
 
     /*
